# .cursorindexingignore — SOFT exclude (search/index only). Files stay openable by the Agent
# and @-mentions on demand; they're just kept out of codebase search & embeddings so they don't
# dilute retrieval quality.
#
# Cursor ALREADY de-indexes (a) everything in .gitignore and (b) a built-in default list (lock
# files, .env*, node_modules/, __pycache__/, build output, images, archives, .git/). So the only
# thing worth listing here is a file that is COMMITTED (indexed by default) yet noisy to embed.
# In this repo that is the dependency lockfile. Everything the previous version also listed
# (htmlcov/, dist/, build/, *.egg-info/, coverage.*, *.log, *.png …) is already gitignored or
# default-ignored — re-listing it was dead weight.

# ── Committed dependency lock — readable for audits, noisy to index/embed ──────
uv.lock

# ── Template hook: if your fork COMMITS generated artifacts Cursor would otherwise index
#    (an OpenAPI dump, a generated client, vendored code), de-index them here, e.g.:
#      openapi.json
#      app/_generated/**
